; Second-round verification after the first token-space board returned REVISE.
; The shared review flow persists every answer before collection.
import "../form/form-stdlib/core.fk"
import "review-panel.fk"
import "review-ask.fk"

(ra-review
  "model/form-neutral-token-space.fk"
  "Second independent verification after the first board returned REVISE; do not edit any file. Read model/form-neutral-token-space.fk, model/tests/form-neutral-token-space-band.fk, model/form-neutral-language-world-model.fk, model/form-neutral-language-world-model-activation.fk, and learn/tests/nl-meaning-net-band.fk. The first board found five executable seams: invalid token spaces could still answer query doors; reversed recipe-to-anchor token edges passed; unordered and empty numeric recipes decoded; graph headers, budgets, and element uniqueness were insufficiently validated; and integer division let 25/50 pass the stated above-twice-chance floor. Freshly preflight the changed cells and run the token-space band. Re-offer an invalid space carrying an unbacked edge and verify resolution and projection are empty; reverse an edge; forge missing-header, negative-budget, and duplicate-element worlds; decode unordered, duplicate, empty, bad-tag, and invalid-anchor coordinates; verify canonical nested anchor/recipe round-trips; and probe unknown surfaces. Verify nml-beats-twice-chance? rejects 25/50 and accepts 26/50, while the band still records rather than hides the raw 34/26/32/36 non-monotonic curve. Confirm the activation sentence fragment is repaired and that bounded-shard worlds remain allowed without claiming completeness. Return PASS AS A BOUNDED CANDIDATE TOKEN/NUMERIC COORDINATE INTEGRATION, REVISE, or BLOCK with executable evidence. Empty or unfinished output is absence, not a vote.")
